# WHAT IS NOT KEPT HERE, AND WHY, SO THE ABSENCE IS NOT MISTAKEN FOR AN OVERSIGHT.
# Same rule as results/holdout_cascade/.gitignore, with one difference recorded at the end.
#
# `stages/cascade_rows.jsonl` is subtract_known.py's per-read row dump, 17 MB per seed. It is
# an intermediate on the way to tiers.json, keyed by the stage manifest's content hash, and
# the same class of file as `results/*/work/` which this repo already ignores. Every removal
# percentage rests on tiers.json and tier_table.json, kept for every seed.
run_s*/stages/cascade_rows.jsonl

# The per-contig and per-read row dumps. Kept for SEED 1 ONLY, as gzip, because one seed's
# rows should be inspectable rather than merely described.
#
# THE DIFFERENCE FROM THE HOLDOUT DIRECTORY, and it is a property of this library rather
# than a change of policy: `contigs.jsonl` is one row per unidentifiable contig, and this
# assembly has 194,703 of them against the holdout's few thousand - 79 MB per seed plain,
# 3.7 MB gzipped. Five seeds plain would be 395 MB in a repo whose whole results tree is
# 583 MB. So seed 1's three dumps are committed compressed and the rest are not committed;
# the uncompressed run directory for every seed is in S3 at the path the launch manifest
# records, and the report names it.
run_s*/contigs.jsonl
run_s*/reads.jsonl
run_s*/layers.jsonl
run_s*/*.jsonl.gz
!run_s1/contigs.jsonl.gz
!run_s1/reads.jsonl.gz
!run_s1/layers.jsonl.gz

# removal_evidence.tsv is the identification table the shortlist stage reads, 20 MB plain
# and 5 MB gzipped, written once for the whole library rather than per seed. Kept, as gzip.
removal_evidence.tsv
